  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive an integer array `cards` where `cards[i]` represents the **value** of the `ith` card. A pair of cards are **matching** if the cards have the **same** value.\n\nOutput *the **smallest** number of **consecutive** cards you have to pick up to have a pair of **matching** cards among the picked cards.* If it is impossible to have matching cards, output `-1`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: cards = [3,4,2,3,4,7]\nOutput: 4\nExplanation: We can pick up the cards [3,4,2,3] which contain a matching pair of cards with value 3. Note that picking up the cards [4,2,3,4] is also optimal.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: cards = [1,0,5,3]\nOutput: -1\nExplanation: There is no way to pick up a set of consecutive cards that contain a pair of matching cards.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= cards.length <= 105`\n* `0 <= cards[i] <= 106`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
